# TestJavaToCSharpTimefoldFacts: timefold-solver's core/main printed as C# with the modification analysis's and the
# NullabilityPass's facts (Policy.KOTLIN), judged by Roslyn (see maddi-run-openjdk's JavaToCSharpRatchet). Lower is
# better for printerCrashes, syntaxErrors, unmappedJdkUses and nullableWarnings, higher for syntaxCleanFiles and
# compilingFiles; `types` must not move. Write a better value here in the commit that earns it.
#
# 2026-10-12, first record, with maddi 3a4a1daf9: the printer is not ready for this corpus yet, nullability is not
# its bottleneck. 611 of 1583 files compile; 8769 errors, most of them generics: 2175 CS0311 (a type argument that
# does not satisfy a constraint, the F-bounded Score_ : IScore<Score_>), 1079 CS0411 (type inference); 2087 unmapped
# JDK uses (RandomGenerator, ToLongFunction, NavigableMap, SequencedMap, ...). 21 syntax errors: ConstraintCollectors
# (8 lines) and an `int` where an expression is expected (5). 504 nullable warnings, many hidden behind the errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, maddi's printer for timefold (maddi 94fd25386: companions of self-bounded types, inner classes,
# explicit type arguments, enum switches, JDK mappings, …): 0 syntax errors, 611 -> 837 compiling files, 8769 -> 3623
# errors, 2087 -> 1379 unmapped JDK uses. 504 -> 571 nullable warnings: no regression, the code that binds now, which
# the errors hid, has its own (the first record's "many hidden behind the errors").
#
# 2026-10-12, maddi e15baf22f: a self-bounded type parameter only a result mentions printed erased, record companions,
# IComparable on a Comparable<Score_>'s companion, T of a Class<T> from the wildcard's bound: 837 -> 868 compiling
# files, 3623 -> 3333 errors. 1379 -> 1380 unmapped JDK uses (NewInstance<ThreadFactory> names the unmapped type).
# 571 -> 579 nullable warnings: CS8602 27 -> 35 on calls that were CS0411 before (stepScope.GetScore().Raw).
#
# 2026-10-12, maddi 21d657e1e (diamond targets, delegate variance, public bases of public types, the type itself in its
# own equals, abstract redeclarations against every ancestor, method group type arguments, inner Slot::new, raw
# constructor references, overrides without constraints): 868 -> 1013 compiling files, 3333 -> 2863 errors, 1380 ->
# 1386 unmapped JDK uses (lambda parameter casts name types already unmapped). 579 -> 601 nullable warnings: CS8603 and
# CS8714 in Joiners and ConstraintCollectors, whose errors went from 134 to 98, so the compiler now reaches them.
#
# 2026-10-12, maddi 2ebe7b7d1: without Gizmo (maddi's timefold-gizmo.csmap leaves its 18 bytecode-generation types out,
# not printed, used through the mapping's rules) and Micrometer as System.Diagnostics.Metrics: 1386 -> 777 unmapped
# uses, 2863 -> 2618 errors, 601 -> 596 nullable warnings. types stays the corpus's 1583; 18 fewer files:
# syntaxCleanFiles 1583 -> 1565, compilingFiles 1013 -> 1007 (8 of the excluded compiled; Micrometer's mapping +2).
#
# 2026-10-13, maddi ff94c0d60: type parameters in scope, navigable and sequenced collections on C#'s sorted and ordered
# ones, JAXB as System.Xml.Serialization with its runtime in the compatibility library (JavaXml.cs), Java resources,
# Math's exact arithmetic and more of the JDK: 777 -> 381 unmapped uses, 1007 -> 1030 compiling files, 2618 -> 2232
# errors. 596 -> 611 nullable warnings: CS8714 +12 and CS8602 +3 in the score collectors (AbstractMinMaxSlot,
# TreeMultiSet, ConnectedRangeChainImpl), whose unconstrained type parameters are now keys of SortedDictionary and
# OrderedDictionary, which want notnull keys (a `where K : notnull` constraint would answer them); the rest in
# GenericJaxbIO and its adapters, newly mapped code that meets System.Xml's annotations.
#
# 2026-10-13, maddi c2be5f33e: a type parameter that is, or is passed as, a dictionary's key is where K : notnull
# (CS8714): 611 -> 594 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-13, maddi ce6ecea39: notnull dictionary keys through wildcards (CS8714 45 -> 19), measured together with
# the JDK nullability hints from JSpecify's annotated JDK (fd3f8419c, merged in the meantime), which move the
# printer's ! assertions throughout: 594 -> 575 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-13, the code review's fixes at maddi e92ecb0f9 (#130): hoisted anonymous constructors typed by the
# superclass constructor, boxed overrides of a type parameter's member, mutually creating inner classes, Math by
# meaning: 1030 -> 1034 compiling files; nullable warnings unchanged (575).
#
# 2026-10-14, the nullability pass's parameter preconditions (CodeLaser/maddi#125, maddi-mod#41): a parameter that its
# method, with its whole override family, dereferences or rejects on every normal exit is non-nullable, and a caller
# that may pass null says !, which does not throw: 575 -> 553 nullable warnings; 1034 compiling files unchanged.
#
# 2026-10-14, the parameter preconditions (CodeLaser/maddi#125, maddi-mod#41): non-nullable where the method,
# with its whole override family, needs the value, ! at a caller that may pass null, not where the method's answer
# to null is an IllegalArgumentException (also through a helper or a constructor); and maddi f779bcd8b: ! on a
